><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250515135834+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250515135836+10'00'" name="9e45075f-b91d-4277-ad6a-39c9ff34a021" page="4" coords="38.097500,347.096000,283.109000,347.096000,38.097500,336.164000,283.109000,336.164000,38.097500,336.154000,283.144000,336.154000,38.097500,325.222000,283.144000,325.222000,38.097500,325.212000,283.140000,325.212000,38.097500,314.280000,283.140000,314.280000,38.097500,314.270000,283.155000,314.270000,38.097500,303.338000,283.155000,303.338000,38.097500,303.271000,283.144000,303.271000,38.097500,292.340000,283.144000,292.340000,38.097500,292.329000,283.154000,292.329000,38.097500,281.398000,283.154000,281.398000,38.097500,281.387000,283.128000,281.387000,38.097500,270.456000,283.128000,270.456000,38.097500,270.388000,283.155000,270.388000,38.097500,259.457000,283.155000,259.457000,38.097500,259.446000,283.145000,259.446000,38.097500,248.515000,283.145000,248.515000,38.097500,248.504000,283.120000,248.504000,38.097500,237.573000,283.120000,237.573000,38.097500,237.505000,85.375100,237.505000,38.097500,226.574000,85.375100,226.574000" rect="37.755900,226.232000,283.497000,347.438000" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Increased age and larger breast size were significantly&#xD;associated with an increased likelihood of elite female athletes&#xD;reporting exercise-induced breast pain. However, despite&#xD;being statistically significant, the logistic regression model&#xD;using age, breast size, BMI, and frequency of sports bra use&#xD;could only weakly predict which athletes did or did not report&#xD;exercise-induced breast pain. The model therefore requires&#xD;substantial improvement in its predictive strength before it can&#xD;serve as a useful tool for coaches and clinicians to identify&#xD;female athletes who may be susceptible to exercise-induced&#xD;breast pain.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="593.972000,255.096000,777.972000,347.096000"
/></highlight
